        "key": "fai2s",
        "text": "august-september 2025, claude. anthropic published a full postmortem. three infrastructure bugs: requests routed to the wrong servers (0.8% of sonnet 4 traffic, peaking around 16% after a load balancing change), a TPU misconfiguration that spat out random thai and chinese characters, and a compiler bug in token sampling. their words:",
        "type": "unstyled"
      },
      {
        "data": {},
        "entityRanges": [],
        "inlineStyleRanges": [],
        "key": "fc53h",
        "text": "We never reduce model quality due to demand, time of day, or server load.",
        "type": "blockquote"
      },
      {
        "data": {},
        "entityRanges": [
          {
            "key": 4,
            "length": 11,
            "offset": 15
          }
        ],
        "inlineStyleRanges": [
          {
            "length": 9,
            "offset": 0,
            "style": "Bold"
          }
        ],
        "key": "2vcg0",
        "text": "the math. theo put it well: if a model does something dumb 1 in 50 times and you send 20 prompts a day, you have a ~33% chance of seeing it on day one. by day five it's ~87%. the model didn't get worse. you just finally rolled the bad dice.",
        "type": "unstyled"
      },
      {
        "data": {},
        "entityRanges": [
          {
            "key": 5,
            "length": 1,
            "offset": 0
          }
        ],
        "inlineStyleRanges": [],
        "key": "ekfku",
        "text": " ",
        "type": "atomic"
      },
      {
        "data": {},
        "entityRanges": [],
        "inlineStyleRanges": [],
        "key": "d887n",
        "text": "look at your effort setting",
        "type": "unordered-list-item"
      },
      {
        "data": {},
        "entityRanges": [],
        "inlineStyleRanges": [],
        "key": "chg3c",
        "text": "check your harness version and what changed in it",
        "type": "unordered-list-item"
      }
